assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

Root cause: `search_products` made a single `GET /products?q=…` call and ignored `next_cursor`, even though the vendor spec has always defined a `cursor` parameter and a `next_cursor` field. The new vendor version (2026-10-01) returns results in pages of 5, so the tool returned 5 items while reporting `total: 7`. The fix keeps requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` and adds each page's items until `next_cursor` is null or missing. v1 responses have `next_cursor: null`, so they still make one request and produce identical output. Typecheck, lint and tests pass, but no 2026-10-01 recording exists, so the cursor requests themselves haven't been tested. One part of the alert is not fixed: the same response has prices 100× the v1 values (p-1101 is 6900 now, 69 in v1), which looks like cents. The spec doesn't mention cents and the response doesn't say which unit it uses, so I left prices unchanged rather than guess a conversion. That still needs confirming with the vendor and its own fix.

